{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgdSsYuAodJsS97oyhW68","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012ejMJiHrGsfAVoaozQKLQu","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"status":"partial","summary":"The syntax for each toolbar button now lives in JavaScript, and the server only sends the button names and how they are grouped. New files app/javascript/wiki_formatting/common_mark.js and textile.js define what each button inserts, plus the table cells and the code block for each precode language. The wiki-toolbar Stimulus controller picks the right file from the new `data-wiki-toolbar-format-value` attribute. It has new `apply` and `insertPrecode` actions and gets the table text from the format file. Its `shortcut` action now checks the modifier keys exactly as the old Stimulus key filters did (only Ctrl, or only Cmd on macOS, with no Shift or Alt). On the Ruby side, each formatter only gives `format` and `button_groups`. Redmine::WikiToolbar renders spacers between groups, gives the table and precode buttons their menus, the help button `wiki-toolbar#help`, the b/i/u shortcuts to strong/em/ins, and the three keyboard actions on the toolbar root. The tests I ran pass: the toolbar unit test, layout_test, wiki_toolbar_test and keyboard_shortcuts_test in a real browser (17 runs, 0 failures), and RuboCop on the changed Ruby files. The full non-system suite (`bin/rails test`) was still running when I had to answer, so I have not confirmed that the whole existing suite passes. Nothing was committed.","changes":[{"path":"app/javascript/wiki_formatting/common_mark.js","summary":"New: what each CommonMark button inserts (wrap or wrapLines, with prefix, suffix, strip and replace), the table header and separator cells, and the precode prefix and suffix for a language."},{"path":"app/javascript/wiki_formatting/textile.js","summary":"New: the same definitions for Textile, with comments that describe the options."},{"path":"config/importmap.rb","summary":"Added pin_all_from for app/javascript/wiki_formatting."},{"path":"app/javascript/controllers/wiki_toolbar_controller.js","summary":"Added the format value and a static formats registry. Replaced the wrap and wrapLines actions with apply({button}). Added insertPrecode({lang}). insertTable now reads the format's table cells. The shortcut action checks for exactly one primary modifier. Removed menuParams."},{"path":"lib/redmine/wiki_toolbar.rb","summary":"Renders the format value, groups of buttons separated by spacers, apply, toggleMenu and help actions, the b/i/u shortcuts and the fixed keyboard actions. Precode menu items now use insertPrecode with a lang param. Removed SPACER, button_params and the per-key shortcut actions."},{"path":"lib/redmine/wiki_formatting/common_mark/helper.rb","summary":"The toolbar now only defines format 'common_mark' and button_groups."},{"path":"lib/redmine/wiki_formatting/textile/helper.rb","summary":"The toolbar now only defines format 'textile' and button_groups."},{"path":"test/unit/lib/redmine/wiki_toolbar_test.rb","summary":"Tests for the format value, the button groups, the apply/menu/help actions, that no syntax params remain, the exact keyboard actions and shortcuts for both formats, and the precode lang params."},{"path":"test/integration/layout_test.rb","summary":"Checks the precode lang params, the format value attribute, and that the importmap pins the wiki_formatting modules."},{"path":"test/system/wiki_toolbar_test.rb","summary":"Added a browser test that clicks every apply button for CommonMark and Textile and checks the inserted text, and a Textile precode test."}],"acceptance":[{"criterion":"The toolbar renders with the new contract for CommonMark and Textile and works the same in the browser","met":true,"evidence":"Unit tests check the format value, the groups and spacers, the apply/button params, the toggleMenu, insertPrecode/lang and help actions, that no prefix/suffix/strip/patte